WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.743
Reflection can happen before action, during action, and after action.

00:00:03.743 --> 00:00:07.387
Reflection before action clarifies goals, assumptions, risks, expectations, and plans.

00:00:07.387 --> 00:00:11.394
Before a project, meeting, incident response, practice session, or design decision,

00:00:11.394 --> 00:00:16.495
a short pre-brief can ask what success looks like, what we expect to happen,

00:00:16.495 --> 00:00:20.502
what could go wrong, and what evidence would change our plan.

00:00:20.502 --> 00:00:24.874
Reflection during action is the skill of noticing while work is underway.

00:00:24.874 --> 00:00:28.518
It means paying attention to confusion, changing conditions, weak signals,

00:00:28.518 --> 00:00:31.068
and gaps between the plan and reality.

00:00:31.068 --> 00:00:35.804
A developer may notice that a debugging theory is not fitting the evidence.

00:00:35.804 --> 00:00:40.176
An incident lead may notice that the room is losing shared understanding.

00:00:40.176 --> 00:00:44.184
A learner may notice that practice has become repetition without attention.

00:00:44.184 --> 00:00:47.827
Reflection after action reviews what happened and what should change.

00:00:47.827 --> 00:00:52.563
An after-action review can examine the goal, the expected outcome, the actual outcome,

00:00:52.563 --> 00:00:55.478
the decisions made, the context, and the lessons.

00:00:55.478 --> 00:00:58.393
The review does not need to be elaborate.

00:00:58.393 --> 00:01:02.765
It needs to be honest enough to identify a future adjustment and

00:01:02.765 --> 00:01:06.044
specific enough that the lesson can be used later.

00:01:06.044 --> 00:01:09.323
Reflection should support action rather than delay it indefinitely.

00:01:09.323 --> 00:01:13.694
A learning loop is useful when it changes preparation, execution, communication, tooling,

00:01:13.694 --> 00:01:14.787
training, or decision-making.

00:01:14.787 --> 00:01:19.159
If reflection becomes endless discussion without changed behavior, it loses practical value.

00:01:19.159 --> 00:01:24.260
The right rhythm is act, notice, learn, adjust, and act again with better information.
